      "lineNbr": 616,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T21:13:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`xs` and `ys` are ordered (top-left, top-right, bot-right, bot-left) or (LRRL) and (TTBB).  The wxyz swizzle shuffles these to (LLRR) and (BTTB) so then the subtraction gives us `(L-L, R-L, R-R, L-R)` and `(T-B, T-T, B-T, B-B)`. These differences work out to the clockwise direction vectors for the left, top, right, bottom edges of the shape. It also generalizes to when the four corners are an arbitrary convex quadrilateral. A similar technique is used throughout the `GrQuadUtils` code on the CPU to handle AA rects in Ganesh.",
      "parentUuid": "2afc79dd_7d659d3b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 616,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 616,
